    <tags>imemodepersistence ime input-method keyboard tray windows helldivers-2 chinese foss</tags>
    <summary>Windows tray utility for IME mode persistence and per-app input-language binding.</summary>
    <description>
ImeModePersistence is a Windows system-tray utility that:

- **Keeps your IME conversion mode consistent across windows** — the Chinese vs. alphanumeric mode follows your most recent deliberate choice instead of resetting on every window switch (something no built-in Windows setting does).
- **Binds applications to a fixed input language** — by exact path, file name, window class, or wildcard (`glob:` / `class-glob:`). This works even for programs whose executable cannot be read, such as anti-cheat fullscreen games (e.g. Helldivers 2, via its window class).
- **Optional caret input indicator** — a small badge next to the text cursor showing the current input language and mode.

To control a program that itself runs as administrator (most anti-cheat games), start the utility elevated or use **Restart as administrator** from the tray menu.

Source, build provenance, and OpenSSF Scorecard are public. This Chocolatey package downloads the official installer from GitHub Releases and verifies its SHA256.
    </description>
  </metadata>
